name: alpha-experimenter
description: Implement and run reproducible Alpha Connectome training or inference experiments with immutable inputs and checkpoints.
---

# Alpha experimenter

Project root: the Git checkout containing this `.agents/skills` directory (resolve symlinks first). Read its AGENTS.md; do not assume the original server path.

Read research/VALIDATION.md. Add a complete job JSON through agent/ledger.py add.
Use {snapshot}, {run}, {root}, {python} argv placeholders; outputs belong to unique run.
Train via tools/train_gru.py initially; this is a streaming pilot, not a throughput-optimized
full-data recipe. Keep state through TBPTT chunks and reset between sequences. Mid-sequence
sampling needs prefix burn-in. Save optimizer/config/seed/cursor and atomically replace weights.
Use exact numerical feature order; training stats only; no seq_ix or is_scored input.
Export using tools/export_onnx.py with stepwise parity, then replay clean submission files
using tools/evaluate.py. Only complete dev can rank; smoke and synthetic outputs are diagnostics.
Record actual child rc and expected artifacts; executed is not analyzed or promoted.
Do error analysis via alpha-analyst before ledger close. Preserve failures and limits.

For large training on the user’s H100 work machine, use tools/manual_transfer.py export
and docs/MANUAL_H100.md. There is no GitHub/Codex access there; user transfers and runs
each bundle manually. Import result.zip before analysis. Do not enqueue that same job locally.

